  "verdict": {
    "summary": "At this fixed seed and route, a low-frequency organismal bauplan acts as a strong inheritance carrier: successive body-attached modules are added without re-solving the creature's overall identity. The annular comparator also yields a coherent organism, so this assay does not show that weak hierarchy necessarily causes horror; it shows that elaborate visible loci without a shared developmental scaffold produce a different, less conventionally grounded body schema and weaker membership in the intended crawler family.",
    "supportedClaims": [
      "The shared bauplan survives two staged elaborations with unusually high visual identity retention.",
      "The dorsal series and paired terminal fork are independently controllable enough to become legible attached anatomy.",
      "The comparator's annulus and proliferated loci remain load-bearing in the generated organism."
    ],
    "unsupportedClaims": [
      "Developmental hierarchy universally prevents grotesque outputs.",
      "The result generalizes across seeds, prompts, cameras, or morphology families.",
